        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nick Broomfield, Gregory Greene, Sandi Sissel, Mother Teresa\n- Films: Chicken Ranch, The End of Suburbia, Mother Teresa (1986), Mr. and Mrs. Smith\n- Places: Pahrump, Nevada, Toronto\n- Organizations/Shows: 60 Minutes\n- Concepts: peak oil, suburban lifestyle\n\nFacts:\n- Chicken Ranch is a 1983 documentary film by Nick Broomfield about the legalised brothel Chicken Ranch in Pahrump, Nevada.\n- Mother Teresa (1986) is a film associated with Sandi Sissel.\n- The End of Suburbia: Oil Depletion and the Collapse of The American Dream is a 2004 documentary film written and directed by Toronto-based filmmaker Gregory Greene.\n- The End of Suburbia concerns peak oil and its implications for the suburban lifestyle.\n- Sandi Sissel is associated with Chicken Ranch, the television show 60 Minutes, and the feature film Mr. and Mrs. Smith.",
